790: - `--execute` requires `autonomy.merge = "auto"` or `--user-approved "<User's words>"`, stored in `approvals`. Otherwise `merge_approval_required`, checked before any state change or Notice. A PR/MR merge also requires the selected review evidence at `gated_sha` (D03) and the latest observation for that request to match `gated_sha`, have checks `SUCCESS`, a review other than `CHANGES_REQUESTED` or `REVIEW_REQUIRED`, and mergeability `MERGEABLE`; otherwise refuse with `checks_not_green` and wait for `merge_ready`. Target freshness is checked only when `defaults.require_current_target = true` (User-only, default `false`). When it is off, a green, `MERGEABLE` PR merges while behind its target, clean-but-behind PRs receive no instruction and no merge queue is used; a PR the forge reports `CONFLICTING` emits `pr_conflict`, and its done or merging Worker is queued an instruction to merge `origin/<target>`, resolve conflicts, republish and signal done again. When it is on, Posse checks target freshness before recording the merge head and again before accepting final CI evidence. Full-pipeline PRs whose candidate becomes stale also enter the target's FIFO merge queue when this setting is off. The queue orders by each Task's latest done Signal; only its head receives a refresh instruction and reruns validation against the latest target. Other queued PRs retain their last green check observation and receive no target-moved instruction until promoted. A promoted head refreshes against the latest target before it can be gated for merge. During a PR watch it refreshes the frozen target before and after the forge observation; a target advance during CI marks that observation `STALE`, not green evidence, and obsoletes any pending `merge_ready` Decision. If the target tip is missing from the PR head, the Task enters its target's FIFO merge queue, keyed by Project, Member and frozen target and ordered by done Signal, and only the queue head's Worker receives an instruction to merge `origin/<target>` into the Task branch, resolve conflicts, republish through the Task's delivery mode and signal done again. This covers clean-but-behind and conflicting branches and does not require the Lead to notice or send a follow-up. Other queued Tasks stay `done` or `merging` with no Worker turn or CI rerun until promoted; `posse merge` on one refuses with `pr_branch_behind` naming its position and the head. The head keeps its place while its instruction is in flight. It is dequeued when its PR merges, when its fresh head fails required checks (re-entering at the back after a later done Signal or green checks), or when its Task leaves `done` and `merging` without an in-flight instruction; the next entry is then promoted. `posse`, `posse list` and `posse show` report `merge_queue` positions. The queue is recorded in [ADR 0031](adr/0031-serialize-target-updates-through-a-merge-queue.md). No-mistakes recovery uses `--skip=rebase` after the Worker has merged the target so a pushed branch is not rebased. Before merging, Posse refreshes the Task's frozen target under the repository sync lock and names the missing commit in `pr_branch_behind`; it never merges a gated head without the current target tip. When that instruction is queued or already delivered, `pr_branch_behind` says so, including on a later `--execute` that finds the Task reopened without a gated head; the Lead waits for the Worker's done Signal instead of sending a duplicate. A Task state change by another actor during Merge, such as a Worker starting a queued fix turn, returns retryable `task_state_changed` naming the public Task ID. The forge merge remains pinned to `gated_sha`. Local fast-forward merges claim the target Git ref and, when the Project root checkout is the target worktree, its canonical path; the claims remain until the merge effect is reconciled. These checks apply with User approval and `autonomy.merge = "auto"` alike. The current-target requirement is recorded in [ADR 0019](ad